# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data, not source. modlists/ alone is ~19 GB of .wabbajack files and
# manifest_backups/ holds superseded copies of the same.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
modlists/
manifest_backups/

# Local Python. .python/ is an interpreter kept inside the project (a
# python-build-standalone unpack) for machines with no Python installed;
# setup_env.bat installs the requirements straight into it, so no venv is
# needed and the folder can move. .venv-win/ is the arrangement for a
# machine-wide Python instead. .mingit/ is the same idea as .python/ for git:
# a MinGit unpack, with the portable Git Credential Manager inside it, and
# git.bat in the project root in front of it. Nothing is installed machine-wide.
.python/
.mingit/
git.bat
.venv-win/
lib-win/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The environment that builds the binaries, and PyInstaller's scratch space.
# Both are made from requirements-build.txt and WabbajackWizard.spec.
.venv-build/
build/

# Your settings. wj_settings.example.json is the documented template; this
# is your copy of it and stays local.
wj_settings.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Never commit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
nexus_api_key.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime state and output, regenerated on every run.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
wj_autoupdate_state.json
wj_manifest_cache.json
wj_overview.json
*.log
*.out
*.csv
*.lock
.nxm_listener_port
.nxm_prev_handler
nxm_captured.txt

# Release builds, made by release.py from what git tracks.
dist/

# A build unzipped or copied here to run beside the data, which is where it
# has to sit: everything it reads is in the folder it starts from.
WabbajackWizard.exe
WabbajackWizard-console.exe
WabbajackWizard*.exe.config
_internal/

# Wabbajack itself, kept inside the project so the whole arrangement moves as
# one. Its launcher downloads each version into a subfolder; the wizard
# removes the superseded ones.
Wabbajack/

# Pre-change copies kept locally for rollback.
.orig_backup_*/

# This share is also mounted from a Mac, and Windows leaves its own litter.
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Backups taken by a live test before damaging real archives.
.test_backup/

# Before/after snapshots written by a verification run.
park_before.json

# The download window's own browser profile: its login to Nexus and its
# cookies, kept here so the whole arrangement stays inside the folder.
.webview/

# collections2mo2, which builds a Nexus collection's MO2 instance: a pinned
# commit checked against a checksum, its libraries in site/, and the 7-Zip,
# MO2 and Root Builder downloads it caches in tools/. wj_collection.py
# setup-c2mo2 rebuilds all of it.
.c2mo2/
.c2mo2.new/
.c2mo2.new.zip*

# Mod Organizer's release archive, pinned by SHA-256, which wj_mo2.py lays
# into every instance the Wizard builds itself; fetched again when missing.
.mo2cache/

# Wabbajack's published validation reports, cached so the browse stage can
# say how much of a list you already hold without downloading its
# .wabbajack. ~45 MB, entirely re-fetchable: wj_autoupdate.py --gallery
# --sync-reports rebuilds it.
.gallery-cache/
